---
title: Sequence Diagram — User Registration Flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User as 👤 User (Browser)
    participant React as React SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant KC as Keycloak
    participant US as User Service
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant KAFKA as Kafka
    participant NS as Notification Service
    participant ES as Elasticsearch

    Note over User,ES: Step 1: User fills registration form in React SPA

    User->>React: Fill form (email, name, password)
    React->>React: Client-side validation
    React->>GW: POST /api/v1/users<br/>{email, firstName, lastName, password}

    Note over GW,KC: Step 2: API Gateway validates JWT (for admin-created users) or allows public registration

    GW->>GW: Rate limit check (Redis sliding window)
    GW->>US: Forward request to User Service

    Note over US,PG: Step 3: User Service processes registration with DDD

    US->>US: Validate CreateUserRequest<br/>(Jakarta Bean Validation)
    US->>US: Create Email Value Object<br/>(self-validates format)
    US->>PG: SELECT EXISTS(email)<br/>Check duplicate email
    PG-->>US: false (not duplicate)
    US->>US: BCrypt.encode(password)<br/>(12 rounds)
    US->>US: User.create(email, name, hash, role)<br/>Factory method → Aggregate Root
    US->>US: Domain Event: UserCreatedEvent registered
    US->>PG: INSERT INTO users (...)<br/>Flyway-managed schema
    PG-->>US: User saved with UUID

    Note over US,ES: Step 4: Publish Domain Events via Kafka

    US->>KAFKA: Publish UserCreatedEvent<br/>Topic: user-events
    US-->>GW: 201 Created<br/>{id, email, name, role, status}
    GW-->>React: 201 Created + UserResponse
    React-->>User: Show success message<br/>Redirect to dashboard

    Note over KAFKA,ES: Step 5: Async Event Consumers process the event

    KAFKA->>NS: Consume UserCreatedEvent
    NS->>NS: ExecutorService.submit()<br/>(Multi-threaded processing)
    NS->>NS: Compose welcome email
    NS-->>User: 📧 Send welcome email

    KAFKA->>ES: Consume UserCreatedEvent
    ES->>ES: Index user for search<br/>{name, email, role}

    Note over User,ES: ✅ Registration Complete — User can now login via Keycloak
